fix(mcp): a dead error branch is dead wherever it is written (#207)

CI's branch-coverage gate caught one one-directional condition:

  internal/mcp/observesession.go:741:5: condition "err == nil" was 31 times
  true but never false

json.Marshal cannot fail for a struct of plain strings. #207 knew that and
folded the marshal error into the MkdirAll branch so there would be no dead
error path of its own. The instinct was right and the construction was not: it
moved the undriveable half onto `err == nil`, which no input can make false.

The error is now dropped explicitly, and what the branch was protecting against
moves to where that risk actually lives. The concern was this type growing a
member that does not encode -- a change to the struct, so it is caught by a test
over the struct. TestObserveSessionMarkerAlwaysEncodes walks every field by
reflection, fails if one is not a string, and round-trips a fully populated
marker. Adding a channel or a func now fails a test rather than silently writing
an empty marker.

That is a better guard than the branch was: the branch would only have fired at
runtime, on a deployment, after the bad member was already shipped.

Driven by the gate's own output, observed failing before the change and green
after, with all five surfaces back at 100% branch.

